

{% liquid
  assign enable_rtl = false
  if request.locale.iso_code == 'ar'
    assign enable_rtl = true
  endif

  assign body_classes = 'template-' | append: template.name | append: ' ' | append: template.suffix | append: ' m-gradient m-color-' | append: settings.default_color_scheme
  if settings.page_transition
    assign body_classes = body_classes | append: ' m:overflow-hidden'
  endif
  if template.suffix == 'about-us'
    assign body_classes = body_classes | append: ' sf__page-about'
  endif
%}
<!doctype html>
<html
  class="no-js {% if settings.page_transition %} m:overflow-hidden{% endif %}"
  lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}"
  data-template="{{ template.name }}"
  {% if enable_rtl %}
    dir="rtl"
  {% else %}
    dir="ltr"
  {% endif %}
>
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=0">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="{{ settings.color_primary }}">
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.shopifycdn.com" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cdn.shopify.com" crossorigin>

    {%- if settings.use_favicon == true and settings.favicon != blank -%}
      <link rel="shortcut icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, height: 32 }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      SEO foundation (2026-08-09; 2026-08-09c CORRECTION: 30ml→20ml business
      change reverted, meta description formulas below restored to "10ml &
      30ml" per explicit user correction). Title format: homepage gets a
      crafted, keyword-informed title; every other page keeps Shopify's own
      page_title (which already respects an explicit Admin SEO title if the
      merchant ever sets one, falling back to the resource's own title
      otherwise) with a " | RAQI" suffix instead of the previous " – {{
      shop.name }}" suffix, since shop.name is "Raqi" (mixed case) and the
      brand's own wordmark/copy is consistently "RAQI" (all caps).

      raqi_page_title (plain-text, no HTML entities) mirrors the same logic
      for reuse in OG/Twitter tags below — fixes a bug where og:title on the
      homepage was falling back to shop.name ("Raqi") because Shopify's raw
      page_title global still resolves to shop.name on index regardless of
      what the <title> tag itself displays.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign raqi_page_title = blank
      if template.name == 'index'
        assign raqi_page_title = "RAQI — Luxury Fragrance Decants UAE | Niche & Designer Perfumes"
      else
        assign raqi_page_title = page_title
        unless raqi_page_title contains 'RAQI' or raqi_page_title contains 'Raqi'
          assign raqi_page_title = raqi_page_title | append: ' | RAQI'
        endunless
      endif
    -%}
    <title>
      {%- if template.name == 'index' -%}
        RAQI &mdash; Luxury Fragrance Decants UAE | Niche &amp; Designer Perfumes
      {%- else -%}
        {{- page_title -}}
        {%- if current_tags -%}
          {%- assign meta_tags = current_tags | join: ', ' %} &ndash; {{ 'general.meta.tags' | t: tags: meta_tags -}}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; {{ 'general.meta.page' | t: page: current_page }}{% endif -%}
        {%- if template == 'password' -%}
          {{- shop.name -}}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- unless page_title contains 'RAQI' or page_title contains 'Raqi' %} | RAQI{% endunless -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </title>

    {%- comment -%}
      Meta description (2026-08-09, revised; 2026-08-09c CORRECTION: "20ml"
      reverted back to "30ml" in the formulas below — the earlier business
      change is undone). IMPORTANT distinction: Shopify's blended
      `page_description` global auto-falls-back to a raw truncation of the
      resource's body content (e.g. product.description) even when no
      explicit Admin SEO description was ever set — confirmed live this was
      silently overriding the crafted, keyword-informed copy below for every
      product. Fixed by checking each resource's own `.seo.description`
      field directly (the TRUE explicit-override signal, confirmed blank on
      every product/collection right now) instead of the blended global, so
      the crafted fallback actually renders until/unless the merchant sets a
      real custom SEO description in Admin. Every branch is kept under 160
      characters by construction, with a truncate as a hard safety net.

      2026-08-09e: the homepage branch's "Dhs 999" is now consolidated —
      whichever branch runs, the result is passed through a `replace` filter
      that swaps a literal "999" for settings.raqi_free_shipping_threshold
      (Theme Settings > Raqi), same single source of truth as the
      announcement bar, PDP shipping accordion and cart progress bar. Only
      the index branch currently contains "999", so this is a safe no-op
      for every other branch.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign raqi_meta_description = blank
      case template.name
        when 'index'
          assign raqi_meta_description = "Try niche and designer perfumes in the UAE before you commit. Authentic 10ml & 30ml decants, hand-poured from the bottle. Free UAE delivery over Dhs 999."
        when 'product'
          assign raqi_meta_description = product.seo.description
          if raqi_meta_description == blank
            assign raqi_meta_description = product.title | append: " decant — 10ml & 30ml, 100% authentic, hand-poured in the UAE. Try it before you commit to the bottle."
          endif
        when 'collection'
          assign raqi_meta_description = collection.seo.description
          if raqi_meta_description == blank
            if collection.handle == 'all' or collection.handle == blank
              assign raqi_meta_description = "Niche & designer perfume decants in the UAE — 10ml & 30ml, 100% authentic. Try before you commit to the full bottle."
            elsif collection.title == 'Niche'
              assign raqi_meta_description = "Niche perfume decants in the UAE — rare and exclusive fragrance houses, 10ml & 30ml, 100% authentic. Try before you commit to the full bottle."
            else
              assign raqi_meta_description = "Niche & designer perfume decants for " | append: collection.title | append: " in the UAE — 10ml & 30ml, 100% authentic. Try before you commit to the full bottle."
            endif
          endif
        when 'page'
          assign raqi_meta_description = page.seo.description
          if raqi_meta_description == blank
            if template.suffix == 'about-us'
              assign raqi_meta_description = "RAQI is a UAE niche & luxury fragrance house — authentic decants poured from the bottle, so you can live with a scent before buying it in full."
            elsif template.suffix == 'contact'
              assign raqi_meta_description = "Questions about sizing, authenticity or delivery? Reach RAQI on WhatsApp or email — a real person answers, usually within a couple of hours."
            endif
          endif
        else
          assign raqi_meta_description = page_description
      endcase
      assign raqi_ship_threshold = settings.raqi_free_shipping_threshold | default: 999
      assign raqi_meta_description = raqi_meta_description | replace: '999', raqi_ship_threshold | strip_html | truncate: 157
    -%}
    {%- if raqi_meta_description != blank -%}
      <meta name="description" content="{{ raqi_meta_description | escape }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- liquid
      render 'social-meta-tags', raqi_page_title: raqi_page_title, raqi_meta_description: raqi_meta_description
      render 'raqi-structured-data'
      render 'font-face'
      render 'critical-css'

      echo 'main.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true

      render 'style-tags'
    -%}

    <script src="{{ 'vendor.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    <script src="{{ 'theme-global.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    {%- if settings.animations != 'none' -%}
      <script src="{{ 'animations.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if request.design_mode -%}
      <script src="{{ 'theme-editor.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    {%- endif -%}

    {{ content_for_header }}
   
    

    <script>
      document.documentElement.className = document.documentElement.className.replace('no-js', 'js');
      if (Shopify.designMode) {
        document.documentElement.classList.add('shopify-design-mode');
      }
    </script>
    {% render 'theme-data' %}
    {% render 'custom-code-head' %}

    {%- comment -%}
      Raqi perf audit (2026-07-30): removed unconditional loads of
      product-page.css (~166KB), compaign.css (~140KB), compaign-v1.css
      (~62KB), compaignv-v2.css (~3.6KB) and the cdnfonts.com/Inter
      stylesheet. Verified 100% unused by Raqi's active pages: these are
      compiled Tailwind/CSS-module bundles (hashed classnames, --tw-*
      vars, Neuzeit-Grotesk font) from an old page-builder feature, with
      zero overlap with any raqi-*/m-* class used in the 6 active
      templates. product-page.css/compaign.css also contain the exact
      `button,[type=submit]{background-color:transparent}` reset that
      caused the earlier Add-to-Cart color bug (worked around via
      !important in custom-code-head.liquid, which stays in place as a
      safety net). Files themselves are left untouched in the theme.
    {%- endcomment -%}

  </head>

  <body
    id="m-theme"
    class="{{ body_classes }} template-{{ template | replace: '.', '-' | replace: '/', '-' }}"
    {% if template.name == 'product' %}
      data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
    {% endif %}


  >
    {%- liquid
      render 'page-transition'
      render 'scroll-top-button'
      sections 'header-group'
    -%}

    <main role="main" id="MainContent">
      {{ content_for_layout }}
    </main>

    
    {%- liquid
      sections 'footer-group'
      render 'script-tags'
      render 'cookie-banner'
      render 'custom-code-body'
    -%}

    <script src="{{ 'product-quick-view.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

    {%- comment -%}
      Raqi perf audit (2026-07-30): removed unconditional wishlist.js and
      compare-product.js. Confirmed both features are fully off in the
      active UI: header-group.json sets show_wishlist_icon=false and
      show_compare_icon=false (so header.liquid never renders those
      icons), settings_data.json sets show_compare_button=false, and
      snippets/product-card-1.liquid hardcodes show_wishlist_button=false
      for every card. No reachable button anywhere calls into either
      script. product-quick-view.js is kept above: show_quickview_button
      defaults true and is not overridden, so the Quickview button is a
      genuinely live feature on product cards.
    {%- endcomment -%}

    {%- if settings.enable_predictive_search -%}
      <script src="{{ 'predictive-search.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if linklists['gift-wrapping'].links != blank
      and linklists['gift-wrapping'].links.first.type == 'product_link'
    -%}
      <script src="{{ 'gift-wrapping.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if settings.show_swatch_option -%}
      <script src="{{ 'product-card-swatch.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      2026-09-03: the Minimog cart drawer ({% render 'cart-drawer' %}, gated on
      settings.enable_cart_drawer) is no longer rendered. The redesign ships its
      own drawer in sections/rd-cart-drawer.liquid via header-group, and having
      both meant Add to Bag opened one drawer and the header's Bag link opened
      the other. assets/cart.js went with it; /cart still loads what it needs
      from sections/cart-template.liquid.
    {%- endcomment -%}


    {%- comment -%}
      2026-09-03 (pre-launch perf pass): removed an inline script that fetched
      /cart.js every 2 seconds, forever, on every page, to update
      .m-cart-count-bubble — an element that only exists in the Minimog header
      (sections/header.liquid), which this theme no longer renders. The live
      header is sections/rd-header.liquid; its bag count is [data-rd-bagcount]
      and sections/rd-cart-drawer.liquid updates it after every cart change.
    {%- endcomment -%}

  </body>
</html>
